#, no-wrap
msgid "Dependency injection and container"
msgstr "Inyección de dependencias y contenedor"

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dependency injection"
msgstr "Inyección de dependencias"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "There are two ways of re-using things in OOP: inheritance and composition."
msgstr "Hay dos formas de reutilizar código en la programación orientada a objetos: la herencia y la composición."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Inheritance is simple:"
msgstr "La herencia es sencilla:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"class Cache\n"
"{\n"
"    public function getCachedValue($key)\n"
"    {\n"
"        // ..\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"final readonly class CachedWidget extends Cache\n"
"{\n"
"    public function render(): string\n"
"    {\n"
"        $output = $this->getCachedValue('cachedWidget');\n"
"        if ($output !== null) {\n"
"            return $output;\n"
"        }\n"
"        // ...        \n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"class Cache\n"
"{\n"
"    public function getCachedValue($key)\n"
"    {\n"
"        // ..\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"final readonly class CachedWidget extends Cache\n"
"{\n"
"    public function render(): string\n"
"    {\n"
"        $output = $this->getCachedValue('cachedWidget');\n"
"        if ($output !== null) {\n"
"            return $output;\n"
"        }\n"
"        // ...        \n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "The issue here is that these two are becoming unnecessarily coupled or inter-dependent, making them more fragile."
msgstr "El problema es que estas dos clases quedan acopladas o son interdependientes sin necesidad, lo que las hace más frágiles."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Another way to handle this is composition:"
msgstr "Otra forma de resolverlo es la composición:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"interface CacheInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    public function getCachedValue($key);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"final readonly class Cache implements CacheInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    public function getCachedValue($key)\n"
"    {\n"
"        // ..\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"final readonly class CachedWidget\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(\n"
"        private CacheInterface $cache\n"
"    )\n"
"    {\n"
"    }\n"
"    \n"
"    public function render(): string\n"
"    {\n"
"        $output = $this->cache->getCachedValue('cachedWidget');\n"
"        if ($output !== null) {\n"
"            return $output;\n"
"        }\n"
"        // ...        \n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"interface CacheInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    public function getCachedValue($key);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"final readonly class Cache implements CacheInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    public function getCachedValue($key)\n"
"    {\n"
"        // ..\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"final readonly class CachedWidget\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(\n"
"        private CacheInterface $cache\n"
"    )\n"
"    {\n"
"    }\n"
"    \n"
"    public function render(): string\n"
"    {\n"
"        $output = $this->cache->getCachedValue('cachedWidget');\n"
"        if ($output !== null) {\n"
"            return $output;\n"
"        }\n"
"        // ...        \n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "We've avoided unnecessary inheritance and used `CacheInterface` in the `CacheWidget` to reduce coupling.  You can replace cache implementation without changing `CachedWidget` so it's becoming more stable. The less edits are made to the code, the less chance of breaking it."
msgstr "Hemos evitado una herencia innecesaria y hemos usado `CacheInterface` en `CacheWidget` para reducir el acoplamiento. Puedes sustituir la implementación de la caché sin cambiar `CachedWidget`, por lo que la clase se vuelve más estable. Cuantas menos modificaciones se hacen en el código, menos probabilidades hay de romperlo."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "The `CacheInterface` here is a dependency: a contract our object needs to function. In other words, our object depends on the contract."
msgstr "Aquí, `CacheInterface` es una dependencia: un contrato que nuestro objeto necesita para funcionar. Dicho de otro modo, nuestro objeto depende del contrato."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "The process of putting an instance of a contract into an object (`CachedWidget`) is called dependency injection.  There are many ways to perform it:"
msgstr "El proceso de introducir una instancia de un contrato en un objeto (`CachedWidget`) se llama inyección de dependencias. Hay muchas formas de hacerlo:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Constructor injection. Best for mandatory dependencies."
msgstr "Inyección por constructor. Es la mejor opción para las dependencias obligatorias."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Method injection. Best for optional dependencies."
msgstr "Inyección por método. Es la mejor opción para las dependencias opcionales."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Property injection. Better to be avoided in PHP except maybe data transfer objects."
msgstr "Inyección por propiedad. En PHP es mejor evitarla, salvo quizá en los objetos de transferencia de datos (DTO)."

#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use private properties"
msgstr "Por qué usar propiedades privadas"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "In the composition example above, note that the `$cache` property is declared as `private`."
msgstr "En el ejemplo de composición anterior, fíjate en que la propiedad `$cache` se declara como `private`."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "This approach embraces composition by ensuring objects have well-defined interfaces for interaction rather than direct property access, making the code more maintainable and less prone to certain types of mistakes."
msgstr "Este enfoque favorece la composición, ya que garantiza que los objetos tengan interfaces bien definidas para interactuar en lugar de permitir el acceso directo a sus propiedades, lo que hace que el código sea más fácil de mantener y menos propenso a ciertos tipos de errores."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "This design choice provides several benefits:"
msgstr "Esta decisión de diseño ofrece varias ventajas:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "**Encapsulation**: Private properties with getters/setters allow you to control access and make future changes without breaking existing code."
msgstr "**Encapsulación**: las propiedades privadas con getters/setters te permiten controlar el acceso y hacer cambios en el futuro sin romper el código existente."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "**Data integrity**: Setters can validate, normalize, or format values before storing them, ensuring properties contain valid data."
msgstr "**Integridad de los datos**: los setters pueden validar, normalizar o formatear los valores antes de guardarlos, lo que garantiza que las propiedades contengan datos válidos."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "**Immutability**: Private properties enable immutable object patterns where setter `with*()` methods return new instances rather than modifying the current one."
msgstr "**Inmutabilidad**: las propiedades privadas permiten patrones de objetos inmutables en los que los métodos setter `with*()` devuelven nuevas instancias en lugar de modificar la actual."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "**Flexibility**: You can create read-only or write-only properties or add additional logic to property access later."
msgstr "**Flexibilidad**: puedes crear propiedades de solo lectura o de solo escritura, o añadir más adelante lógica adicional al acceso a las propiedades."

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "DI container"
msgstr "Contenedor DI"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Injecting basic dependencies is straightforward. You're choosing a place where you don't care about dependencies, which is usually an action handler, which you aren't going to unit-test ever, create instances of dependencies needed and pass these to dependent classes."
msgstr "Inyectar dependencias básicas es sencillo. Eliges un lugar en el que no te preocupen las dependencias, que suele ser un manejador de acción al que nunca vas a hacer pruebas unitarias, creas las instancias de las dependencias necesarias y se las pasas a las clases dependientes."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "It works well when there are few dependencies overall and when there are no nested dependencies. When there are many and each dependency has dependencies itself, instantiating the whole hierarchy becomes a tedious process, which requires lots of code and may lead to hardly debuggable mistakes."
msgstr "Funciona bien cuando hay pocas dependencias en total y no hay dependencias anidadas. Cuando hay muchas y cada dependencia tiene a su vez sus propias dependencias, instanciar toda la jerarquía se convierte en un proceso tedioso, que requiere mucho código y puede provocar errores difíciles de depurar."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Additionally, lots of dependencies, such as certain third-party API wrappers, are the same for any class using it.  So it makes sense to:"
msgstr "Además, muchas dependencias, como ciertos envoltorios (wrappers) de API de terceros, son las mismas para cualquier clase que las use. Por eso tiene sentido:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Define how to instantiate such common dependencies."
msgstr "Definir cómo instanciar esas dependencias comunes."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Instantiate them when required and only once per request."
msgstr "Instanciarlas cuando se necesiten y solo una vez por solicitud."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "That's what dependency containers are for."
msgstr "Para eso sirven los contenedores de dependencias."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "A dependency injection (DI) container is an object that knows how to instantiate and configure objects and all objects they depend on."
msgstr "Un contenedor de inyección de dependencias (DI) es un objeto que sabe cómo instanciar y configurar objetos y todos los objetos de los que estos dependen."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Yii provides the DI container feature through the [yiisoft/di](https://github.com/yiisoft/di) package and [yiisoft/injector](https://github.com/yiisoft/injector) package."
msgstr "Yii ofrece la funcionalidad de contenedor DI mediante los paquetes [yiisoft/di](https://github.com/yiisoft/di) y [yiisoft/injector](https://github.com/yiisoft/injector)."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> [!NOTE]\n"
"> The container contains only shared instances. If you need a factory, use the dedicated\n"
"> [yiisoft/factory](https://github.com/yiisoft/factory) package.\n"
msgstr ""
"> [!NOTE]\n"
"> El contenedor solo contiene instancias compartidas. Si necesitas una factoría, usa el paquete específico\n"
"> [yiisoft/factory](https://github.com/yiisoft/factory).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> [!TIP]\n"
"> [Martin Fowler's article](https://martinfowler.com/articles/injection.html) has well\n"
"> explained why DI container is useful. Here we will mainly explain the usage of the DI container provided by Yii.\n"
msgstr ""
"> [!TIP]\n"
"> El [artículo de Martin Fowler](https://martinfowler.com/articles/injection.html) explica muy bien\n"
"> por qué es útil un contenedor DI. Aquí explicaremos principalmente cómo usar el contenedor DI que proporciona Yii.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuring container"
msgstr "Configurar el contenedor"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Because to create a new object you need its dependencies, you should register them as early as possible.  You can do it in the application configuration, `config/web.php`. For the following service:"
msgstr "Como para crear un objeto nuevo necesitas sus dependencias, conviene registrarlas lo antes posible. Puedes hacerlo en la configuración de la aplicación, `config/web.php`. Para el siguiente servicio:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"final class MyService implements MyServiceInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(int $amount)\n"
"    {\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    public function setDiscount(int $discount): void\n"
"    {\n"
"    \n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"final class MyService implements MyServiceInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(int $amount)\n"
"    {\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    public function setDiscount(int $discount): void\n"
"    {\n"
"    \n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "configuration could be:"
msgstr "la configuración podría ser:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"return [\n"
"    MyServiceInterface::class => [\n"
"        'class' => MyService::class,\n"
"        '__construct()' => [42],\n"
"        'setDiscount()' => [10],\n"
"    ],\n"
"];\n"
msgstr ""
"return [\n"
"    MyServiceInterface::class => [\n"
"        'class' => MyService::class,\n"
"        '__construct()' => [42],\n"
"        'setDiscount()' => [10],\n"
"    ],\n"
"];\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "That's equal to the following:"
msgstr "Esto equivale a lo siguiente:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$myService = new MyService(42);\n"
"$myService->setDiscount(10);\n"
msgstr ""
"$myService = new MyService(42);\n"
"$myService->setDiscount(10);\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "You can provide arguments with names as well:"
msgstr "También puedes pasar los argumentos con nombre:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"return [\n"
"    MyServiceInterface::class => [\n"
"        'class' => MyService::class,\n"
"        '__construct()' => ['amount' => 42],\n"
"        'setDiscount()' => ['discount' => 10],\n"
"    ],\n"
"];\n"
msgstr ""
"return [\n"
"    MyServiceInterface::class => [\n"
"        'class' => MyService::class,\n"
"        '__construct()' => ['amount' => 42],\n"
"        'setDiscount()' => ['discount' => 10],\n"
"    ],\n"
"];\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "That's basically it. You define a map of interfaces to classes and define how to configure them. When an interface is requested in constructor or elsewhere, container creates an instance of a class and configures it as per the configuration:"
msgstr "Básicamente, eso es todo. Defines un mapa de interfaces a clases e indicas cómo configurarlas. Cuando se solicita una interfaz en un constructor o en otro lugar, el contenedor crea una instancia de la clase y la configura según lo indicado en la configuración:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"final class MyAction\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(\n"
"        private readonly MyServiceInterface $myService\n"
"    ) {\n"
"    }\n"
"    \n"
"    public function __invoke() \n"
"    {\n"
"        $this->myService->doSomething();\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"final class MyAction\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(\n"
"        private readonly MyServiceInterface $myService\n"
"    ) {\n"
"    }\n"
"    \n"
"    public function __invoke() \n"
"    {\n"
"        $this->myService->doSomething();\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "There are extra methods of declaring dependency configuration."
msgstr "Hay otras formas de declarar la configuración de las dependencias."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "For simplest cases where there are no custom values needed and all the constructor dependencies could be obtained from a container, you can use a class name as a value."
msgstr "En los casos más sencillos, en los que no se necesitan valores personalizados y todas las dependencias del constructor pueden obtenerse del contenedor, puedes usar un nombre de clase como valor."

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"interface EngineInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    \n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"final class EngineMarkOne implements EngineInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(CacheInterface $cache) {\n"
"    }   \n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"interface EngineInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    \n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"final class EngineMarkOne implements EngineInterface\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(CacheInterface $cache) {\n"
"    }   \n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "In the above example, if we already have cache defined in the container, nothing besides the class name is needed:"
msgstr "En el ejemplo anterior, si ya tenemos la caché definida en el contenedor, no hace falta nada más que el nombre de la clase:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"return [\n"
"    // declare a class for an interface, resolve dependencies automatically\n"
"    EngineInterface::class => EngineMarkOne::class,\n"
"];\n"
msgstr ""
"return [\n"
"    // declara una clase para una interfaz y resuelve las dependencias automáticamente\n"
"    EngineInterface::class => EngineMarkOne::class,\n"
"];\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "If you have a dependency that has public properties, you can configure it as well."
msgstr "Si tienes una dependencia con propiedades públicas, también puedes configurarlas."

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"final class NameProvider\n"
"{\n"
"    public string $name;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"final class NameProvider\n"
"{\n"
"    public string $name;\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Here's how to do it for the example above:"
msgstr "Así se hace para el ejemplo anterior:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"NameProvider::class => [\n"
"    'class' => NameProvider::class, \n"
"    '$name' => 'Alex',\n"
"],\n"
msgstr ""
"NameProvider::class => [\n"
"    'class' => NameProvider::class, \n"
"    '$name' => 'Alex',\n"
"],\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "In this example, you may notice `NameProvider` specified twice. The key is what you may request as dependency and the value is how to create it."
msgstr "En este ejemplo, quizá notes que `NameProvider` se especifica dos veces. La clave es lo que puedes solicitar como dependencia y el valor es cómo crearla."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "If the configuration is tricky and requires some logic, a closure can be used:"
msgstr "Si la configuración es complicada y requiere cierta lógica, puedes usar un closure:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MyServiceInterface::class => static function(ContainerInterface $container) {\n"
"    return new MyService($container->get('db'));\n"
"},\n"
msgstr ""
"MyServiceInterface::class => static function(ContainerInterface $container) {\n"
"    return new MyService($container->get('db'));\n"
"},\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Additionally, to `ContainerInterface`, you can request any registered service directly as a closure parameter.  The injector will automatically resolve and inject these:"
msgstr "Además de `ContainerInterface`, puedes solicitar directamente cualquier servicio registrado como parámetro del closure. El inyector los resolverá e inyectará automáticamente:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"MyServiceInterface::class => static function(ConnectionInterface $db) {\n"
"    return new MyService($db);\n"
"},\n"
msgstr ""
"MyServiceInterface::class => static function(ConnectionInterface $db) {\n"
"    return new MyService($db);\n"
"},\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "It's possible to use a static method call:"
msgstr "Se puede usar una llamada a un método estático:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "MyServiceInterface::class => [MyFactory::class, 'create'],\n"
msgstr "MyServiceInterface::class => [MyFactory::class, 'create'],\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Or an instance of an object:"
msgstr "O una instancia de un objeto:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "MyServiceInterface::class => new MyService(),\n"
msgstr "MyServiceInterface::class => new MyService(),\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Injecting dependencies properly"
msgstr "Inyectar dependencias correctamente"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Directly referencing a container in a class is a bad idea since the code becomes non-generic, coupled to the container interface and, what's worse, dependencies are becoming hidden.  Because of that, Yii inverts the control by automatically injecting objects from a container in some constructors and methods based on method argument types."
msgstr "Hacer referencia directamente a un contenedor dentro de una clase es una mala idea, ya que el código deja de ser genérico, queda acoplado a la interfaz del contenedor y, lo que es peor, las dependencias quedan ocultas. Por eso, Yii invierte el control inyectando automáticamente objetos desde un contenedor en algunos constructores y métodos según los tipos de sus argumentos."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "This is primarily done in constructor and handing method of action handlers:"
msgstr "Esto se hace principalmente en el constructor y en el método que procesa la acción de los manejadores de acción:"

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"use \\Yiisoft\\Cache\\CacheInterface;\n"
"\n"
"final readonly class MyController\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(\n"
"        private CacheInterface $cache\n"
"    )\n"
"    {\n"
"        $this->cache = $cache;    \n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    public function actionDashboard(RevenueReport $report)\n"
"    {\n"
"        $reportData = $this->cache->getOrSet('revenue_report', function() use ($report) {\n"
"            return $report->getData();               \n"
"        });\n"
"\n"
"        return $this->render('dashboard', [\n"
"           'reportData' => $reportData,\n"
"        ]);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"use \\Yiisoft\\Cache\\CacheInterface;\n"
"\n"
"final readonly class MyController\n"
"{\n"
"    public function __construct(\n"
"        private CacheInterface $cache\n"
"    )\n"
"    {\n"
"        $this->cache = $cache;    \n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    public function actionDashboard(RevenueReport $report)\n"
"    {\n"
"        $reportData = $this->cache->getOrSet('revenue_report', function() use ($report) {\n"
"            return $report->getData();               \n"
"        });\n"
"\n"
"        return $this->render('dashboard', [\n"
"           'reportData' => $reportData,\n"
"        ]);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/concept/di-container.md
msgid "Since it's [yiisoft/injector](https://github.com/yiisoft/injector) that instantiates and calls action handler, it checks the constructor and method argument types, gets dependencies of these types from a container and passes them as arguments. That's usually called auto-wiring. It happens for sub-dependencies as well, that's if you don't give dependency explicitly, the container would check if it has such a dependency first.  It's enough to declare a dependency you need, and it would be got from a container automatically."
msgstr "Como es [yiisoft/injector](https://github.com/yiisoft/injector) quien instancia y llama al manejador de acción, comprueba los tipos de los argumentos del constructor y del método, obtiene del contenedor las dependencias de esos tipos y las pasa como argumentos. Esto suele llamarse autowiring (conexión automática). También ocurre con las subdependencias: si no proporcionas una dependencia explícitamente, el contenedor comprueba primero si tiene esa dependencia. Basta con declarar la dependencia que necesitas para que se obtenga automáticamente del contenedor."

